#### CATEGORY=Source tree
### Suggests a minimal set of code owners to review a commit.

## Usage: fx min-owners [-v] [--all] [--include-root] [--author EMAIL] [--branch BRANCH] [REV]
##
## Looks up the owners of each file changed in REV (a commit or a range like
## main..HEAD, default HEAD) using Gerrit's code-owners plugin, then finds the
## fewest owners who together cover every file. Run it from inside the git repo
## that the commit belongs to, e.g. vendor/google.
##
## Owners come from OWNERS files on the BRANCH branch, so OWNERS changes in
## the commit itself aren't taken into account.
##
## If more than 5 reviewers are needed, it points to the docs for asking for
## an owners override.
##
## Ties between equally good owners are broken randomly to spread out review
## load. The randomness is seeded by today's date and the commit author, so
## repeated runs on the same day give the same answer. (Very large changes
## fall back to a simpler search that doesn't do this.)
##
## Owners whose calendar says they're out of office, and who won't be back
## within 4 hours, are only suggested for files that nobody else can approve.
## This check uses the prebuilt `luci-auth` (or one on PATH), which works
## without logging in on cloudtops and needs `luci-auth login -scopes-gerrit`
## elsewhere; without it, the check is skipped with a note.
##
## Flags:
##   -v, --verbose     List the files each owner covers
##   --all             List every smallest set of owners instead of just one
##   --include-root    Consider root OWNERS members for every file, not just
##                     for files with no other owners
##   --author EMAIL    Email that gets implicit approval (default: the commit
##                     author); set this if your git email differs from your
##                     Gerrit account's
##   --branch BRANCH   Branch whose OWNERS files to use (default: main)

readonly SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" >/dev/null 2>&1 && pwd)"
source "$SCRIPT_DIR/../lib/vars.sh" || exit $?

exec "${PREBUILT_PYTHON3}" "$SCRIPT_DIR/min_owners.py" "$@"
